LeetCode: Maximal Square
Problem: Maximal Square
Approach: Dynamic Programming (2D DP)
We use a 2D DP array where dp[i][j] represents the maximum side length of a square whose bottom-right corner is at position (i, j).

If the current cell contains '1', we calculate the minimum of its three neighboring cells (top, left, and top-left) and add 1.

DP Transition:
dp[i][j] = 1 + \min(dp[i-1][j], dp[i][j-1], dp[i-1][j-1])

If the current cell contains '0', its DP value remains 0.

We maintain maxi to store the maximum side length found and return its square as the maximum area.
C++ Code
class Solution {
public:
    int maximalSquare(vector<vector<char>>& matrix) {
        int row = matrix.size();
        int col = matrix[0].size();

        vector<vector<int>> area(row, vector<int>(col, 0));
        int maxi = 0;

        for(int i = 0; i < row; i++) {
            for(int j = 0; j < col; j++) {

                if(i - 1 >= 0 && j - 1 >= 0 && matrix[i][j] == '1') {
                    area[i][j] = 1 + min({
                        area[i-1][j],
                        area[i-1][j-1],
                        area[i][j-1]
                    });
                }
                else {
                    matrix[i][j] == '1' ? area[i][j] = 1 : area[i][j] = 0;
                }

                maxi = max(maxi, area[i][j]);
            }
        }

        return maxi * maxi;
    }
};


Complexity Analysis
- Time Complexity: \(O(m \times n)\), as we traverse every cell exactly once.
- Space Complexity: \(O(m \times n)\), for the 2D DP array.
